;;; Ein — mixed value kinds in one hypothesis slot
;;;
;;; Two candidate `seat` facts whose second argument is `1` in one and
;;; `left` in the other, on a KB that is otherwise perfectly well-formed.
;;; **`1` is a name**: a run of digits is one (Q-M1e2.24), so the two
;;; candidates are two names of one kind and sort by text. The file was
;;; written for an int beside a symbol, a kind Ein does not have; it keeps
;;; the shape, and R is four states, every commitment of the two.
;;;
;;; What it pins. Candidates are ordered by *content*
;;; (`Terms::cmp_fact_semantic`): relation name first, then the arguments
;;; element-wise. Two candidates of the same relation whose slot *i* holds a
;;; name in one and a nested fact in the other are compared across value
;;; kinds, and values are totally ordered by construction
;;; (`docs/ein/reasoning/01-static-ir/01-knowledge-base.md` § Order, a total
;;; order), so any such pair sorts like any other.
;;;
;;; Why it uses an hrule. An `hrule`'s `:assert` args come from *bindings*:
;;; a variable that matched a fact's argument carries that value through,
;;; whatever its kind. Hence the shape below — one `hrule`, one variable, two
;;; facts that bind it to `1` and to `left`.
;;;
;;; `ein solve FILE` lists the four states: ∅, `{(seat Ann 1)}`,
;;; `{(seat Ann left)}` and both.
;;;
;;; `nested-fact-hypothesis.ein` is the other half of the same ordering: two
;;; candidates whose argument is a nested `Fact`, with no mixed slot types.
;;;
;;; Pinned by `corpus/corpus.toml` (the sweep runs it under every declared
;;; run, against a banked exit golden) and by `ein-infer/tests/interning.rs`,
;;; which uses it for a second thing: `Ann` is a name only the compiler ever
;;; sees.

(relation slotval T T :why "slot {?1} has the value {?2}")
(relation seat    T T :why "{?1} sits at {?2}")

;; The two bindings. `?v` matches the name `1` from one and the name `left`
;; from the other, and both are candidate `seat` facts.
(slotval x 1)
(slotval y left)

(hrule guess ()
  :match  (slotval ?k ?v)
  :assert (seat Ann ?v)
  :why    "guess that Ann sits at {?v}")

(solve
  :hrules (guess))

(query
  :goal   (seat Ann ?s)
)
